 "purpose": "KV-GRP7 10-20: KV-GRP7 s7 branch slices (388.8 x 388.8): four W->E PC-branch slices (row macro MY rd_out E -> two staggered 4-macro ring stacks A/B MY -> exit flops at E pins), E pins regrouped per branch by exact io_tcl; no ring column in front of the E face, no ring word crosses another ring column; row gap 22.5 um. KV-GRP8 s7c/s7d: ring macro LEF faces by port class (master W = clk/r_*/rd_out/w_mask[15:0], E = w_ce/w_addr/wd_in/w_mask[31:16]; MY -> read port E toward the exits, write port W toward the incoming word); s7a/s7b failed trial GRT with GRT-0183 on ring-B wd_in[3] (write word split over both faces wrapped round the abutted stack ends), also after a fresh-process resume. Same RTL/netlist as s6 (qkd_kvs_grp_s6c), +0 cycles.",
